-- title:
--   Rational scalars built from Γ and a conjugate lie in Γ
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a_2,b_2$ and natural numbers $N,q,q'$ with $N$ nonzero and squarefree, $q$ and $q'$ prime, neither $q$ nor $q'$ dividing $N$, $q'\neq q$, and $q,q'\geq 5$. Assume the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a₂ b₂ q`, that is $a_2<0$, $b_2<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completion $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra (every nonzero element a unit) exactly when $q\in v$. Let $\Lambda_2$ and $R_2$ be $\mathbb Z$-submodules of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]$ with $\Lambda_2$ a maximal order (an order: containing $1$, multiplicatively closed, $\mathbb Q$-spanning the algebra, finitely generated; and maximal among orders containing it), with $R_2$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection $\Lambda_1'\cap\Lambda_2'$ of two maximal orders whose relative index in $\Lambda_1'$ is $N$), and $R_2\leq\Lambda_2$. Let $v_1$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $q'$. Let $\Gamma\leq(\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2])^\times$ be a subgroup whose members are exactly those units $x$ that lie in `awayUnits R₂ v₁` — for every height-one prime $w\neq v_1$, the image of $x$ in $(\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w)^\times$ lies in the subgroup generated by those local units $u$ with $u$ and $u^{-1}$ both in the local box of $R_2$ at $w$ — and for which $\mathrm{padicValRat}\,q'\,(\mathrm{nrd}\,x)$ is even, where $\mathrm{nrd}$ is the reduced norm $x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a_2x_{\mathrm{imI}}^2-b_2x_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2+a_2b_2x_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$. Then for any unit $z$ which is the image of a nonzero rational scalar $c$ under $\mathbb Q\to\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]$, if $z=\delta\,(t^{-1}\gamma t)$ for some $\delta,\gamma\in\Gamma$ and some unit $t$, then $z\in\Gamma$.
--
--   This is the faithfulness statement for the group of $q'$-units of even reduced-norm valuation attached to an Eichler order in the definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q$ and $\infty$: a rational scalar that is a product of an element of $\Gamma$ with a conjugate of an element of $\Gamma$ by an arbitrary quaternion unit is itself in $\Gamma$. It is used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.descentIntertwining_of_base_one_zero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.descentIntertwining_of_base_one_zero), where the kernel of the projective action consists of such rational scalars.
